    "created_at": "2018-05-24T00:30:56Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-05-24T00:30:56Z",
    "body": "Here's a test-case where Firefox right now does trigger a new load, and I'll stop making it do that:\r\n\r\n```html\r\n<!doctype html>\r\n<script>\r\n  window.loads = 0;\r\n  window.errors = 0;\r\n</script>\r\n<picture style=\"display: block\">\r\n  <source media=\"(max-width: 799px)\" srcset=\"green-256x256.png 100w\" sizes=\"22px\">\r\n  <source media=\"(min-width: 800px)\" srcset=\"green-256x256.png 100w\" sizes=\"40px\">\r\n  <img onload=\"console.log(++window.loads)\" onerror=\"console.log(--window.errors)\" style=\"max-width: 100%\">\r\n</picture>\r\n```",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
