    "created_at": "2019-05-21T13:53:00Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-05-21T13:53:00Z",
    "body": "> No UA triggers loads when the selected density changes as a result of the sizes attribute, which doesn't follow the spec, but I think it's the right thing to do.\r\n\r\nChromium actually does trigger those loads when sizes' value is defined as a \"vw\" value, but as you say, it probably shouldn't. Related issue: https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/4646\r\n\r\nSeems like stricter tests are in order...\r\n\r\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
